# Building block view

{% callout type="info" title="About this chapter" %}
The building block view shows the static decomposition of the system into building blocks and their relationships – top-down, level by level. For each building block, describe its purpose and interfaces ("black box").
{% /callout %}

## Level 1

| Building block | Responsibility |
|:---|:---|
| Route planning | Creates and optimizes routes, manages orders |
| Live view | Combines positions and status into a real-time picture |
| Telematics gateway | Normalizes data from different telematics providers |
| Maintenance | Schedules maintenance, exchanges appointments with the workshop portal |
| Analytics | Calculates key figures and costs per vehicle and route |
| App backend | Provides routes to the mobile app and receives status updates |

## Level 2: Telematics gateway

The gateway wraps each provider in its own adapter. All adapters emit events in the common `VehiclePositionReported` format.

```json {% title="Event VehiclePositionReported" %}
{
  "vehicleId": "TRK-0417",
  "timestamp": "2026-10-25T07:42:13Z",
  "position": { "lat": 51.9225, "lon": 4.4792 },
  "speedKmh": 42,
  "source": "telematics-a"
}
```

{% callout type="tip" %}
A new provider only requires one more adapter. All other building blocks remain unchanged.
{% /callout %}
